WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:17.646
I wasn't able to help Jenny with her school problems.

2
00:00:17.647 --> 00:00:23.177
But I had a new invention idea, and it was going to be great.

3
00:00:23.178 --> 00:00:28.301
This invention wouldn't fall into a fish tank or get caught on anyone's sweater.

4
00:00:28.302 --> 00:00:32.119
And there was still time to write about it for Mr. Bright.

5
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:36.933
"What's your idea, Iggy?" asked Jenny as we headed home.

6
00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:42.866
"Did you see the way that ticket machine worked at the bakery?" I asked.

7
00:00:42.867 --> 00:00:47.945
"You mean where you pick a number so you can save your place in line?" asked Molly.

8
00:00:47.946 --> 00:00:50.052
"That's right," I said.

9
00:00:50.053 --> 00:00:53.069
"We could print tickets for the bumpy slide.

10
00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:57.366
Kids would pick a ticket and wait for their number to be called."

11
00:00:57.367 --> 00:01:02.553
"No one would have to stand in line anymore," said Jenny.

12
00:01:02.554 --> 00:01:08.851
I nodded. "Kids could run around the playground until their number was called."

13
00:01:08.852 --> 00:01:13.475
"Your invention is just in time, Iggy," said Josh.

14
00:01:13.476 --> 00:01:18.024
"I heard Mr. Dalmati say that kids were pushing and shoving too much in line.

15
00:01:18.025 --> 00:01:21.514
And no one gets much exercise at recess anymore."

16
00:01:21.515 --> 00:01:23.869
I frowned, thinking.

17
00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:29.651
"I could cut up pieces of cardboard and print the numbers on them," I said.

18
00:01:29.652 --> 00:01:33.717
"Then kids can pick the numbers out of a bag."

19
00:01:33.718 --> 00:01:38.147
Everyone agreed to help print tickets for the slide.

20
00:01:38.148 --> 00:01:42.954
So we went upstairs to my apartment to get some cardboard.

21
00:01:42.955 --> 00:01:48.348
I found some that I had used for a project in school.

22
00:01:48.349 --> 00:01:51.901
Then we went to Molly's apartment.

23
00:01:51.902 --> 00:01:58.612
Molly and Caswell's babysitter, Lucy, had just made some chocolate chip cookies.

24
00:01:58.613 --> 00:02:04.749
The apartment smelled almost as good as Mom's Bakery!

25
00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:09.544
So we all sat down and had warm cookies and lemonade.

26
00:02:09.545 --> 00:02:13.537
After that we got to work.

27
00:02:13.538 --> 00:02:18.219
We cut the cardboard into small squares.

28
00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:24.800
Then we printed big numbers on each square with a magic marker.

29
00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:29.619
We printed numbers all the way up to one hundred.

30
00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:32.766
Everyone helped, even Caswell.

31
00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:38.627
Now during recess kids could pick a number to take a turn on the slide.

32
00:02:38.628 --> 00:02:41.824
"We will need a number caller," I said.

33
00:02:41.825 --> 00:02:45.526
"What's a number caller?" asked Jenny.

34
00:02:45.527 --> 00:02:50.063
"It's the person who calls out the next number," I explained.

35
00:02:50.064 --> 00:02:53.281
"Remember the man at Mom's Bakery?"

36
00:02:53.282 --> 00:02:56.102
Molly grinned and imitated him.

37
00:02:56.103 --> 00:02:59.938
"Number seven is next!"

38
00:02:59.939 --> 00:03:02.364
"Exactly," I said.

39
00:03:02.365 --> 00:03:06.790
"Let's take turns calling out the numbers," said Jenny.

40
00:03:06.791 --> 00:03:11.178
I wanted this to be a really, really good invention.

41
00:03:11.179 --> 00:03:14.404
So I came up with one more idea.

42
00:03:14.405 --> 00:03:18.877
"I'll ask my mom if she'll take us to Dollar Delight," I said.

43
00:03:18.878 --> 00:03:22.215
"They sell lots of cheap little toys.

44
00:03:22.216 --> 00:03:27.050
Kids can pick a number from one bag and a toy from another.

45
00:03:27.051 --> 00:03:29.966
Then they can have fun while they're waiting."

46
00:03:29.967 --> 00:03:34.213
"But won't we run out of toys?" asked Jenny.

47
00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:36.184
"No," I said.

48
00:03:36.185 --> 00:03:41.571
"When the kids turn in their tickets, they'll turn in their toys too."

49
00:03:41.572 --> 00:03:44.314
"Wow," said Molly.

50
00:03:44.315 --> 00:03:47.632
"This is a really great invention, Iggy."

51
00:03:47.633 --> 00:03:50.127
I hoped Molly was right.

52
00:03:50.128 --> 00:03:57.024
My Fabulous Glasses-Finder had sounded like a good idea too—at first.

53
00:03:57.025 --> 00:04:00.776
But my Pick-a-Number invention was different.

54
00:04:00.777 --> 00:04:03.931
It would solve a big problem at school.

55
00:04:03.932 --> 00:04:09.103
Maybe it would even be in Mr. Bright's new book!

56
00:04:09.104 --> 00:04:16.117
After dinner my mom took us to Dollar Delight.

57
00:04:16.118 --> 00:04:20.580
We bought lots of little toys for only about ten dollars.

58
00:04:20.581 --> 00:04:24.097
We also bought two colorful shopping bags.

59
00:04:24.098 --> 00:04:30.240
We planned to fill one shopping bag with tickets and the other with toys.

60
00:04:30.241 --> 00:04:37.930
I could hardly wait until recess the next day!
